  },
  {
    path: 'Bank PO (IBPS, SBI) and other public-sector banking exams',
    bestFor: 'Graduates who want stable, structured government-adjacent work and can commit to a real preparation stretch.',
    reality: 'Open to graduates of any stream, which means the competition is not a commerce-only pool — thousands of engineering and arts graduates sit the same exam.',
  },
  {
    path: 'SSC CGL and other central government exams',
    bestFor: 'Graduates who want roles like Income Tax Inspector, Auditor, or Assistant, with pension-grade job security.',
    reality: 'Genuinely open to any graduate, so a commerce background does not give you an edge on the exam itself — only in the on-the-job work afterward.',
  },
  {
    path: 'Business analyst or data analyst',
    bestFor: 'Graduates who like numbers but want to skip multi-year exam cycles and enter through demonstrated tool skill instead.',
    reality: 'Excel alone will not get you shortlisted anymore. SQL, Power BI, or basic Python plus one real project is what actually separates offers.',
  },
  {
    path: 'Accountant, auditor, or tax associate (direct entry, no further exam)',
    bestFor: 'Graduates who want to start earning immediately and build practical depth on the job.',
    reality: 'The most common first job for BCom graduates, and also the most likely to stay flat in pay if you never add a tool, certification, or specialisation on top.',
  },
  {
    path: 'Digital marketing',
    bestFor: 'Graduates who are commercially minded but do not want a numbers-only role.',
    reality: 'Low entry barrier and a genuine freelance income ceiling, but it rewards a portfolio of real campaigns far more than a certificate on a resume.',
  },
  {
    path: 'Investment banking or wealth management support roles',
    bestFor: 'Graduates who like markets, client conversations, and are comfortable with target-driven work.',
    reality: 'Entry roles are junior and process-heavy; the real income growth needs a few years plus a certification like NISM or CFA Level 1.',
  },
  {
    path: 'E-commerce and business operations',
    bestFor: 'Graduates who think in systems and enjoy coordinating vendors, logistics, and reporting.',
    reality: 'A quiet, underrated entry point at growing D2C and marketplace companies, but it rarely gets mentioned by placement cells.',
  },
  {
    path: 'UGC NET and academic route (after MCom)',
    bestFor: 'Graduates who genuinely want to teach commerce at the college level.',
    reality: 'BCom alone does not qualify you for NET — you need an MCom first, which adds two years before this door even opens.',
  },
  {
    path: 'Entrepreneurship or family business',
    bestFor: 'Graduates with access to a business, capital, or a specific market gap they understand well.',
    reality: 'Ownership has the highest ceiling of any path here, but it also has the least structure — you need finance, sales, and operations skill built fast, not slowly.',
  },
];

const checkpointItems = [
  {
    num: '01',
    title: 'Work style',
    body: 'Do you want a long, structured exam grind with delayed reward (CA/CS/CMA), a stable but slow-moving government ladder (bank PO, SSC CGL), or a faster skill-first entry where proof of work counts more than a certificate (analytics, digital marketing)?',
    note: 'A path with a great reputation that fights how you actually like to work will not survive the years it demands.',
  },
  {
    num: '02',
    title: 'Context',
    body: 'Can your family absorb 2-5 years of CA or CS preparation with modest or no income, or do you need earning to start within a few months? MCom plus NET is a slower, cheaper route; MBA at a weak institute on a loan is a faster route with real debt risk attached.',
    note: 'The safer plan is the one your household can actually fund end to end, not the one that sounds most respectable at a family function.',
  },
  {
    num: '03',
    title: 'Market',
    body: 'Is there real, current hiring for this specific path, not just a relative\'s success story from a decade ago? Bank PO vacancies, SSC CGL notifications, and analytics job postings are checkable right now; a vague sense that "commerce jobs exist somewhere" is not.',
    note: 'Look at this year\'s actual vacancy count and this month\'s actual job postings before locking in a plan.',
  },
  {
    num: '04',
    title: 'Survival',
    body: 'Will this path still need you once AI tools get better at the routine parts of it? Routine bookkeeping, basic reconciliation, and first-draft reports are already being automated. Judgment, client communication, and strategic interpretation are not.',
    note: 'Choose the version of the path where you own a decision or a relationship, not just a spreadsheet cell.',
  },
];

const gateItems = [
  {
    num: 'Gate 1',
    title: 'Proof of skill',
    body: 'Take one CA/CS/CMA mock paper, build one small Excel or Power BI dashboard, or run one mock digital marketing campaign plan. Produce something small in the path before you commit years to it.',
  },
  {
    num: 'Gate 2',
    title: 'Proof of communication',
    body: 'Explain in under two minutes why this specific path fits your work style and your family\'s financial runway, not why it sounds impressive to relatives.',
  },
